   "text": "Who We Are Applied Materials is the global leader in materials science and engineering solutions that are at the foundation of virtually every new semiconductor chip and advanced display in the world. The equipment that we create and service is essential to advancing AI and accelerating the commercialization of next-generation semiconductor chips. Join us and push the boundaries of materials science and engineering in a company at the foundation of the electronics industry. The work we do together advances the world’s technology. What We Offer Location: Bundang,KOR You’ll benefit from a supportive work culture that encourages you to learn, develop, and grow your career as you take on challenges and drive innovative solutions for our customers. We empower our team to push the boundaries of what is possible—while learning every day in a supportive leading global company. Visit our Careers website to learn more. At Applied Materials, we care about the health and wellbeing of our employees. We’re committed to providing programs and support that encourage personal and professional growth and care for you at work, at home, or wherever you may go. Learn more about our benefits . About the Role We are seeking an experienced Financial Analyst to support the Applied Global Services (AGS) business in Korea. This role serves as a key finance partner to business leaders and cross-functional teams, providing financial planning, forecasting, profitability analysis, and decision support for a dynamic semiconductor services business. The position requires a strong combination of financial analysis, business acumen, and cross-functional collaboration. The successful candidate will translate complex business and operational data into actionable financial insights and support management decisions across revenue growth, profitability, customer contracts, and strategic business initiatives. Key Responsibilities Lead and support revenue, bookings, gross margin, and business performance forecasting, including quarterly Forecast cycles and other planning cycles. Partner closely with Sales, Business Development, Field Service Operations, and other cross-functional teams to validate business assumptions and ensure financial forecasts appropriately reflect customer and operational developments. Analyze actual performance versus forecast and plan, identify key business drivers, risks and opportunities, and provide clear management commentary. Develop financial models and scenario analyses to support strategic planning, business sizing, revenue outlook, profitability improvement, and management decision-making. Perform customer and contract-level profitability analysis, including revenue, cost, gross margin, commercial credits, pricing changes, and other financial implications. Provide Finance support for new deals, contract renewals, pricing decisions, and commercial proposals, ensuring consistency among pricing, costs, margin assumptions, and P&L impacts. Monitor business trends and translate operational drivers such as customer demand, installed base growth, service activity, shipments, and business mix into financial impacts. Identify and communicate financial risks and opportunities across revenue and gross margin, and work with business partners to develop appropriate actions. Prepare financial analysis and executive-level commentary for Finance and non-Finance management reviews. Support quarter-end financial activities, including close, flash, commit, forecast updates, and variance analysis. Drive or participate in finance process improvement, reporting enhancement, system integration, and analytical automation initiatives. Maintain strong financial controls and data integrity while exercising sound judgment across multiple sources of financial and operational information. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics, Business Administration, or a related discipline Relevant experience in FP&A, business finance, comme",
